From 3a3e13da789be0ceda21c4167d506254d1865e1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oblivios <oblivios@localhost>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:13:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] oblivios: add the Duress Unlock set-up flow, main and
 set-up screens and the Device unlock row

oblivios: add the Duress Unlock set-up flow and its tests

Orders the set-up, change and remove steps of the decoy without Android
types so it runs on the JVM: create, start without a credential, set the
PIN, stop with delayed locking, register last; a failed set-up unregisters
and removes the user; remove clears the registration before the user.

oblivios: add the Duress Unlock main and set-up screens and the Device unlock row

Adds the row below Duress password (order 1010, system user only), the
main screen, the set-up and change screen, the Android adapter of the
flow, the strings and the manifest entries. Both activities finish at
once for any user but the system user, so a decoy session cannot open
them. A candidate PIN is checked against the wipe PIN through
isDuressWipeCredential and never through checkCredential.
